{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"code":"Bundle.module","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}]},{"text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and add a ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Overriding text per-app","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builder closures (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAnnouncement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own. ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"announcement.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates","kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenStates","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Give any screen a standard ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Empty"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Loading"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"text":" state, usable from both UIKit and SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateView":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstateview","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Renders the right content for a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", switching between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Empty \/ Loading \/ Data \/ Error automatically.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateView"}],"title":"ScreenStateView","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentat